Assignment 4 — Research: DevOps and CI/CD for Machine
Learning
Aim: Explain how DevOps practices improve ML development and deployment.
Write these points in your practical record
• DevOps: A set of practices that brings development and operations together through automation, collaboration,
testing, deployment, and monitoring.
• CI (Continuous Integration): Automatically build and test code changes whenever developers push or merge code.
• Continuous Delivery: Keep tested software ready to release; a person may approve production deployment.
• Continuous Deployment: Automatically release every change that passes the pipeline to production.
• Version control: Git tracks source code, configuration, and changes. Large datasets and model files may need
dedicated data/model versioning.
• Automated testing: Unit tests, API tests, data validation, and model checks catch defects early.
• Containerization: Docker packages the app and dependencies to reduce 'works on my machine' problems.
• Model monitoring: Track API availability, latency, errors, resource use, prediction quality, and data/model drift.
• Reproducibility: Record dependencies, code revision, dataset version, model parameters, and model artifact.
• Rollback: Keep a previous known-good image/model so a failed deployment can be reversed.
Example ML CI/CD flow
Developer pushes code
|
v
GitHub
|
v
Jenkins detects change
|
v
Install dependencies + run tests
|
v
Build Docker image
|
v
Deploy to test environment
|
v
