|
v
Deploy / promote to production
|
v
Monitor API, model, data and resources
ML-specific issues to mention
• Passing software tests does not guarantee model quality; add checks for accuracy or other task-specific metrics.
• Training data can change over time, causing data drift or concept drift.
• A model may be correct but too slow or memory-heavy for production.
• Protect secrets, personal data, model artifacts, and deployment credentials.
• Separate model training from model serving where appropriate.
Conclusion: CI/CD makes ML releases repeatable and faster, while testing, model/data tracking, monitoring, and
rollback improve reliability.

